		"nodes": {
			"32": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "OR \/ XOR \/ NOR\n\nOR, XOR and NOR are logic gates. They only accept booleans as input. \nOR outputs true when either or both inputs are true. \nXOR(exclusive or) ouputs true when either inputs are true, but false when both inputs are true.\nNOR(not or) outputs true when both inputs are false.\n\n- Patch Explained -\n\n•  We have two booleans going into the left and right input of each logic gate.\n•  Join makes sure we can use instances in this patch.\n•  If a channel turns true the If node turns the true into a trigger that triggers the Attack Release node.\n•  The Attack Release is connected to the height of the squares.\n•  The red square jumps up if OR turns true.\n•  The same is true for XOR (green) and NOR (blue)."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 329.523284912109375,
					"width": 713.99993896484375,
					"x": -322.423004150390625,
					"y": -192.19451904296875
